        <title>Observables</title>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                The role of linear operators in quantum mechanics is to measure the physical properties of a system
                (called <term>observables</term>). They are defined such that we can compute the expected value of
                the given observable in state <m>\psi(x)</m> using the inner product:
